e-16 factors, chosen among the sixteen to maximise the longest run of consecutive residues it leaves out. The single-block logicals form the cyclic code of dimension 16 whose zeros are the 241 residues the divisor leaves out, and the Bose-Chaudhuri-Hocquenghem bound on that run puts the lightest single-block logical well above this claim; a direct circulant search at 12 seeds of 600,000 trials finds nothing below 84. Draws with two even weights are rejected, since (x + 1) divides a binary polynomial exactly when its weight is even and would add the root-1 coset to the common gcd. The distance is a witness-backed upper bound from a 24-seed gate at 2,000,000 information-set trials per seed; the orbit fold over every equal-orbit partition of the qubits returns nothing lighter."}}